      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1", "C9"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2", "C9.1", "C9.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "Net-(C9-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C1 is 0.1uF/16V and C9 is 1nF/25V in the netlist.",
      "expected": "Both C1 and C9 should be 1uF/25V according to the design specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C9\") (value \"1nF/25V\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD driver's charge-pump and display power filtering will have incorrect capacitance values, potentially causing unstable boost converter operation or improper e-paper panel power sequencing.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.13", "U5.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U5 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "These Ethernet PHY differential pair pins should not be tied directly to ground; they should be connected to the RJ45 jack or left unconnected/terminated per standard practice.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U5 | SKYLAB SKW92A ... 5-port Ethernet switch"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting the Ethernet transmit outputs to ground can damage the SKW92A PHY or at least prevent that Ethernet port from functioning, and is a non-standard termination for unused ports.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor (libsource Device:C) but its footprint is an inductor footprint (Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder). Additionally, C11.1 is on the net 'unconnected-(C11-Pad1)' and C11.2 is on GND.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint, and both pins should be connected to the intended circuit (e.g., a power rail and ground) to provide decoupling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitor cannot be assembled on the inductor footprint, and even if it were, it is not connected to any signal, so it provides no decoupling or circuit function.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: C1 and C9 have incorrect values compared to the specification, U5 Ethernet transmit pins 13 and 14 are shorted to ground, and C11 is a capacitor with an inductor footprint and an unconnected pin."
}

